(947, 1, '2024-12-08 05:59:20', '2024-12-08 05:59:20', '<h2> GIVEING IS\n CARING\n</h2>		\n		<p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. .</p>		\n													<img width=\"736\" height=\"489\" src=\"http://localhost/ngo/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/50-Heartwarming-Photos-That-Will-Give-You-Hope.jpeg\" alt=\"\" />													\n			<h2>EMPOWERING PWDs  WITH LOVE </h2>		\n		<p>Love is a powerful force. It’s not just about affection, but about showing respect, understanding, and care for others. For PWDs, love means seeing them as individuals with unique strengths, talents, and aspirations, rather than defining them solely by their disability.</p><p>When we empower PWDs with love, we create spaces where they feel accepted and encouraged. It\'s about cultivating a culture where:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Access to Opportunities</strong>: With love comes the responsibility to ensure equal opportunities. Everyone deserves a chance to pursue their goals, whether it\'s education, employment, or social activities. Love means advocating for accessible spaces, inclusive workplaces, and education systems that cater to all needs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Support and Understanding</strong>: People with disabilities often face societal misconceptions or biases. By showing love, we help break these barriers, promoting empathy and understanding. This means providing emotional support, offering help when needed, and celebrating their achievements.</p></li><li><p><strong>Self-Love and Confidence</strong>: Empowering PWDs with love also means teaching them to love themselves. Through encouragement and support, they can build the confidence to pursue their dreams, advocate for themselves, and live independently.</p></li><li><p><strong>Community and Connection</strong>: Love brings people together. It means building a network of individuals and organizations that work to create more inclusive communities. From creating social groups to offering resources, when we extend love to PWDs, we help them feel connected and part of society.</p></li><li><p><strong>Breaking Barriers</strong>: Disabling is not the condition itself, but the barriers society puts in place. When we empower PWDs with love, we actively work to dismantle these obstacles, whether they are physical, social, or attitudinal.</p></li></ol>		\n			<h2>GALLERY</h2>		\n			<figure class=\'gallery-item\'>\n				<a data-elementor-open-lightbox=\"yes\" data-elementor-lightbox-slideshow=\"8935efa\" data-elementor-lightbox-title=\"Wood burning stove\" data-e-action-hash=\"#elementor-action%3Aaction%3Dlightbox%26settings%3DeyJpZCI6NjcsInVybCI6Imh0dHA6XC9cL2xvY2FsaG9zdFwvbmdvXC93cC1jb250ZW50XC91cGxvYWRzXC8yMDI0XC8xMVwvaXN0b2NrcGhvdG8tNTA4MjIyOTU2LTEwMjR4MTAyNC0yLmpwZyIsInNsaWRlc2hvdyI6Ijg5MzVlZmEifQ%3D%3D\" href=\'http://localhost/ngo/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/istockphoto-508222956-1024x1024-2.jpg\'><img width=\"1024\" height=\"682\" src=\"http://localhost/ngo/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/istockphoto-508222956-1024x1024-2.jpg\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-67\" decoding=\"async\" /></a>\n				<figcaption class=\'wp-caption-text gallery-caption\' id=\'gallery-1-67\'>\n				Wood burning stove\n				</figcaption></figure><figure class=\'gallery-item\'>\n				<a data-elementor-open-lightbox=\"yes\" data-elementor-lightbox-slideshow=\"8935efa\" data-elementor-lightbox-title=\"Incomplete Spinal Cord Injury Recovery Time_ What to Expect\" data-e-action-hash=\"#elementor-action%3Aaction%3Dlightbox%26settings%3DeyJpZCI6NDA2LCJ1cmwiOiJodHRwOlwvXC9sb2NhbGhvc3RcL25nb1wvd3AtY29udGVudFwvdXBsb2Fkc1wvMjAyNFwvMTJcL0luY29tcGxldGUtU3BpbmFsLUNvcmQtSW5qdXJ5LVJlY292ZXJ5LVRpbWVfLVdoYXQtdG8tRXhwZWN0LmpwZyIsInNsaWRlc2hvdyI6Ijg5MzVlZmEifQ%3D%3D\" href=\'http://localhost/ngo/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Incomplete-Spinal-Cord-Injury-Recovery-Time_-What-to-Expect.jpg\'><img width=\"735\" height=\"490\" src=\"http://localhost/ngo/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Incomplete-Spinal-Cord-Injury-Recovery-Time_-What-to-Expect.jpg\